course: dictionary
lesson: 2104
title: A hired worker for a job
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A contractor is a person or company that is paid to do a job, usually building or repair work, under an agreement. The agreement is a promise about what will be done and how much it will cost. A contractor is hired for the job. They are not a regular worker who comes in every day.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The building contractor fixed our roof in three days.» Building and roof tell you the kind of job, and fixed tells you the contractor did the work. The phrase «hire a contractor» points the same way: someone is paid to do a job.
explain: Some phrases add extra meaning. «Independent contractor» means a worker who does not have the rights and benefits of an employee, such as sick pay and holiday pay. Swap in your meaning to check: "The roof was fixed by a person hired to do the job." That still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A contractor is a person or company paid to do a job under an agreement.
fact: «Contractor» often means someone who builds or repairs things, like houses, roofs and roads.
fact: A contractor is hired for a job for a set time, not as a regular employee.
fact: «Independent contractor» means a worker without the rights and benefits of an employee, such as sick pay and holiday pay.
fact: Useful phrases: building contractor, hire a contractor, independent contractor.
exercise: «The building contractor fixed our roof in three days.» What is a contractor? | A kind of roof tile | A person who always stays at home | *Someone who is paid to do a job under an agreement | A pupil who is good at drawing
exercise: Mum says, «We will hire a contractor to lay the new road.» What does hire mean here? | To teach someone to read | To sell our old house | *To pay someone to do a job for us | To borrow a car for the day
exercise: «An independent contractor does not get sick pay or holiday pay.» Which is true? | *Contractors are not regular employees, so they miss out on those benefits | Contractors are always paid more than employees | Contractors always work in a school | They get holiday pay as well as sick pay
test: A contractor is best described as | A type of tool | A regular employee who never changes jobs | *A person hired to do a job under an agreement | A street sign
test: Which sentence uses contractor correctly? | The contractor sang a song at the party | *We hired a contractor to build our garage | Contractors are a kind of bird | I went to the contractor to see the sea
exam: Which phrase describes a worker without the rights and benefits of an employee? | Holiday pay | *Independent contractor | Building contractor | Safe job
